<title>MOROCCO: Islamic Bank grants Morocco $10 mln to boost trade.</title>
<headline>Islamic Bank grants Morocco $10 mln to boost trade.</headline>
<dateline>CASABLANCA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia-based Islamic Development Bank on Monday granted Morocco's leading Banque Marocaine du Commerce Exterieur a $10 million loan to boost trade between Rabat and Islamic countries.</p>
<p>In a statement received on Monday, the Casablanca-based BMCE said: &quot;The loan will be devoted to finance Morocco's foreign trade with Islamic countries.&quot;</p>
<p>The loan will cover mainly imports such as crude oil and Moroccan exported phosphates products, it said.</p>
<p>($1= 9.5 dirhams)</p>
